{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Cressida Curzon Bonas (born 18 February 1989) is an English actress, dancer and model.","title":"Cressida Bonas"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" She is the youngest daughter of Lady Mary-Gaye Curzon and entrepreneur Jeffrey Bonas, and a granddaughter of Edward Curzon, 6th Earl Howe.","title":"Cressida Bonas"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Bye Bye Man is a 2017 American supernatural horror film directed by Stacy Title and written by Jonathan Penner, based on the chapter "The Bridge to Body Island" in Robert Damon Schneck's book "The President's Vampire".","title":"The Bye Bye Man"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The film stars Douglas Smith, Lucien Laviscount, Cressida Bonas, Doug Jones, Carrie-Anne Moss, Faye Dunaway and Jenna Kanell.","title":"The Bye Bye Man"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Bottom of the World is a 2017 drama film.","title":"Bottom of the World (film)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It was directed by Richard Sears, written by Brian Gottlieb and stars Jena Malone, Douglas Smith and Ted Levine.","title":"Bottom of the World (film)"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Lady Alexandra Naldera Curzon, CBE (20 March/April 1904 – 7 August 1995), was the third daughter of George Curzon, 1st Marquess Curzon of Kedleston and Viceroy of India, and Lord Curzon's first wife, the American mercantile heiress, Mary Victoria Curzon, Baroness Curzon of Kedleston (née Leiter).","title":"Lady Alexandra Curzon"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" She was named after her godmother, Queen Alexandra and her place of conception, Naldehra, India.","title":"Lady Alexandra Curzon"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" She and her two older sisters were memorialized by Anne de Courcy in "The Viceroy's Daughters: The Lives of the Curzon Sisters".","title":"Lady Alexandra Curzon"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Gelston Castle, located between Castle Douglas and Kirkcudbright, in Dumfries and Galloway, Great Britain, was built for Sir William Douglas of Castle Douglas, who had acquired the lands of Gelston in 1799.","title":"Gelston Castle"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" However, Sir William Douglas died without issue in 1809 and his property was divided between various nieces and nephews, with Gelston going to the youngest daughter of his brother James, Mathilda Douglas.","title":"Gelston Castle"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" In 1813 Mathilda married William Maitland, and their family continued to preside over the estate for most of the 19th Century.","title":"Gelston Castle"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Gelston then became the property of the Galliers-Pratts who retained the castle for pheasant shooting, and from whom it was requisitioned during World War II.","title":"Gelston Castle"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" During this time it served as a home for handicapped boys evacuated from Glasgow, before the roof was removed once this use had ceased.","title":"Gelston Castle"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"One Night in Istanbul, also known as One Night in Istanbul: The Movie, is a British comedy-drama film, directed by James Marquand and produced/written by Nicky Allt.","title":"One Night in Istanbul"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The film stars Steven Waddington, Paul Barber, Lucien Laviscount, Samantha Womack, and Ingvar Eggert Sigurðsson.","title":"One Night in Istanbul"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" It is based on the play of the same name by Nicky Allt.","title":"One Night in Istanbul"}],"peer_messages":["Unverified peer answer: The Bye Bye Man
