{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Handi-Snacks are a snack food product line sold by Mondelez International.","title":"Handi-Snacks"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The common two-compartment Handi-Snack has a small spread compartment and a larger compartment for crackers; a red plastic spreader is included with crackers.","title":"Handi-Snacks"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Mondelez International, Inc., styled Mondelēz ( ), is an American multinational confectionery, food, and beverage company based in Illinois which employs about 107,000 people around the world.","title":"Mondelez International"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It consists of the global snack and food brands of the former Kraft Foods Inc after the October 2012 spin-off of its North American grocery operations.","title":"Mondelez International"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The Mondelez name, adopted in 2012, was suggested by Kraft Foods employees and is derived from the words "mundus" (Latin for “world”) and "delez" (a proxy for the word "delicious").","title":"Mondelez International"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"PepsiCo, Inc. is an American multinational food, snack, and beverage corporation headquartered in Purchase, New York.","title":"PepsiCo"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" PepsiCo has interests in the manufacturing, marketing, and distribution of grain-based snack foods, beverages, and other products.","title":"PepsiCo"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" PepsiCo was formed in 1965 with the merger of the Pepsi-Cola Company and Frito-Lay, Inc.","title":"PepsiCo"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" PepsiCo has since expanded from its namesake product Pepsi to a broader range of food and beverage brands, the largest of which included an acquisition of Tropicana Products in 1998 and the Quaker Oats Company in 2001, which added the Gatorade brand to its portfolio.","title":"PepsiCo"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Canyon Creek Food Company () is a food processing company based in Edmonton, Alberta that provides fresh soups and other prepared food products geared towards health conscious consumers.","title":"Canyon Creek Food Company"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The company provides its fresh food product line to grocery retailers and a broad range of food service establishments such as restaurants and institutions throughout Canada.","title":"Canyon Creek Food Company"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Twisties are a type of cheese curl, corn-based snack food product, available mainly in Australia, and other Oceanian countries such as Papua New Guinea, New Caledonia, Vanuatu and Fiji, the Southeast Asian countries Malaysia, Thailand, Singapore and Brunei, and the island of Mauritius in the Indian Ocean.","title":"Twisties"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It was launched in 1950 by the General Foods Corporation.","title":"Twisties"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The brand name is owned by The Smith's Snackfood Company.","title":"Twisties"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" While originally an Australian-owned company, Smith's was acquired in August 1998 by Frito-Lay, the second largest producer of snack foods in Australia, which in turn is owned by American multi-national PepsiCo.","title":"Twisties"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" In Malaysia, Twisties is a product of Mondelēz International, after having been a part of Danone and later, Kraft Foods previously.","title":"Twisties"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" In Thailand, the Twisties trademark is owned by Lay's, which like The Smith's Snackfood Company, is owned by PepsiCo.","title":"Twisties"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" In New Zealand, Malta and Italy, Twisties are marketed under different names.","title":"Twisties"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Deep Fried Peanuts are a snack food created by deep frying peanuts in an oil.","title":"Deep-fried peanuts"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The resulting product is a snack food that can be eaten in its entirety, both shell and nut.","title":"Deep-fried peanuts"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The deep-frying process does not change the flavor or texture of